# ArduCopter parameters for the CityLife quad flown in Project AirSim
# (robot_citylife_ardupilot.jsonc, controller "ardupilot-api").
#
# Loaded LAST, after the two files `sim_vehicle.py -v ArduCopter -f airsim-copter`
# loads itself (Tools/autotest/default_params/copter.parm and airsim-quadX.parm,
# read from the pinned Copter-4.5.7 tree). rail.sitl_args() also starts SITL
# with -w, which erases the parameters stored in eeprom.bin by an earlier
# session (a value edited in Mission Planner, say); without -w a stored value
# would override --defaults. With both, every value here wins at every start.
#
#   bash demo/pas_ardupilot/start_ardupilot.sh ...      (what our launcher runs)
#   sim_vehicle.py -v ArduCopter -f airsim-copter --add-param-file=<this file> ...
#                                                        (the upstream equivalent)

# --- 1. Airframe and rate-loop tuning ---------------------------------------
# Quad, X layout: motor 1 front-right, 2 rear-left, 3 front-left, 4 rear-right,
# which is the robot config's actuator-order.
FRAME_CLASS     1
FRAME_TYPE      1
# Main loop at the scene's 200 sensor frames a second (step-ns 5 ms in
# scene_citylife_ardupilot.jsonc). airsim-quadX.parm sets 300, which CityLife
# cannot feed: ArduPilot measured 221-222 Hz on 2026-10-08 and refused to arm.
SCHED_LOOP_RATE 200
# Copied verbatim from IAMAI's project-airsim-quad.param, the tuning their
# ArduPilot example flies this exact airframe with (same mass, links and rotor
# coefficients; tests/test_pas_ardupilot.py checks the airframe identity).
ATC_RAT_RLL_P   0.733
ATC_RAT_RLL_I   0.733
ATC_RAT_RLL_D   0.0056
ATC_ANG_RLL_P   36.000
ATC_ACCEL_R_MAX 374870
ATC_RAT_PIT_P   0.768
ATC_RAT_PIT_I   0.768
ATC_RAT_PIT_D   0.0050
ATC_ANG_PIT_P   36.00
ATC_ACCEL_P_MAX 348730
ATC_RAT_YAW_P   2.000
ATC_RAT_YAW_I   0.200
ATC_RAT_YAW_D   0.0000
ATC_ANG_YAW_P   3.429
ATC_ACCEL_Y_MAX 2893

# --- 2. Autonomous speeds sized to the CityLife policy ----------------------
# airsim-quadX.parm sets WPNAV_SPEED 2000 (20 m/s) and RTL_ALT 2500 (25 m). The
# CityLife policies cap speed at 5 m/s and climb at 2 m/s and hold 6-14 m
# (policies/follow_car_citylife.yaml), so the autopilot's own modes (AUTO for
# the G1 square, RTL as the fence action) stay inside the same envelope the
# Shield enforces on the pilot.
WPNAV_SPEED     500
WPNAV_SPEED_UP  200
WPNAV_SPEED_DN  150
RTL_ALT         1200

# --- 3. The autopilot's own geofence: the grant's "ultimate backstop" -------
# Architecture constraints: "The autopilot's own GeoFence / FENCE_ACTION is the
# ultimate backstop -- the Shield does not replace it, it pre-empts it."
# Maximum altitude 20 m (above the policy's 14 m ceiling, so the Shield acts
# first) and a 400 m circle round home. The radius is sized from flown data:
# over the 26 stored CityLife follow trajectories (demo/out/citylife*/
# trajectory.json, measured 2026-10-07) the largest horizontal distance from
# the start point is 253.7 m (citylife_redcar_final2), and 214 m is typical
# of the red-car runs. A 250 m circle would have fired RTL in the middle of
# such a follow; 400 m leaves about 1.5x margin. tests/test_pas_ardupilot.py
# re-measures it when those runs are on disk. The policy has no keep-in
# boundary, so nothing tighter is pre-empted by the Shield here.
# Action 1 = RTL, or LAND where RTL is impossible.
FENCE_ENABLE    1
FENCE_TYPE      3
FENCE_ALT_MAX   20
FENCE_RADIUS    400
FENCE_ACTION    1

# --- 4. Telemetry on SERIAL0, the link mavlink-router holds ------------------
# Streamed without anyone asking, so Mission Planner, MAVROS and the perception
# node all see position, attitude, EKF status and servo outputs from boot.
# Mission Planner may raise or lower these for the shared link; the perception
# node also requests its own messages by MAV_CMD_SET_MESSAGE_INTERVAL.
SR0_POSITION    10
SR0_EXTRA1      10
SR0_EXTRA2      10
SR0_EXTRA3      2
SR0_EXT_STAT    2
SR0_RC_CHAN     10
